From 728e0b3a3f99bc47ff052c82ef0ef1886a56f57c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grafici patch export <patch-export@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:34:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Define finite range, missing-sample and empty-input contracts

Add explicit valid() queries for Range, DataNorm, normalized sources and
windows. Missing samples use reversed range metadata instead of an ambiguous
zero sentinel; payload stays 12 bytes for float and 6 for Float16. Float16
finite checks inspect exponent bits directly. Legitimate zero and constant
ranges remain valid, with normalized value zero. Reversed/non-finite ranges
are invalid unless explicitly sorted. Range delta uses the computation type.

Arrays/functions discover finite bounds and preserve gaps. Empty linear
sources do not underflow; negative slopes get ordered bounds. Null buffers
and callbacks expose zero size. Histograms reject zero bins at compile time,
skip missing samples, avoid division by zero for empty normalized counts and
reject invalid class layouts. Zero/out-of-range window slices report invalid;
polar subwindows preserve their parent. Interpolation rejects missing knots
and non-finite spline coefficients/evaluations. Plotters skip missing points
or touching segments; palettes reject invalid samples and clamp generated
channels before integer conversion. CONTRACTS.md specifies API behavior.

No validity array, per-sample flag or new heap allocation is added. Validity
is checked at construction where possible and per sample for streamed data.

Validation: data_contracts covers float/FP16, full-width signed/unsigned
ranges, NaN/infinity gaps, empty sources/histograms and invalid windows.
Existing checks and the zero-bin compile-failure fixture pass under UBSan
plus float-cast-overflow. The full FP16 sketch also builds for Uno R3.
